---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro'
import katex from 'katex'

const branches = [
  {
    number: '01',
    name: 'Source',
    role: 'authorized constructibility',
    formula: String.raw`\mathcal S \xrightarrow{\ C\ } \mathcal X`,
    formulaLabel: 'Source S maps by constructor C to carrier X',
    status: 'labelled provenance required',
  },
  {
    number: '02',
    name: 'Comparison',
    role: 'bidirectional observation',
    formula: String.raw`\mathcal X \underset{R}{\overset{F}{\rightleftarrows}} \mathcal Y`,
    formulaLabel: 'Carrier X and carrier Y joined by forward map F and reverse map R',
    status: 'residual coherence stays typed',
  },
  {
    number: '03',
    name: 'Completion',
    role: 'stability under enlargement',
    formula: String.raw`\widehat{\mathcal X}=\varprojlim_{F}\mathcal X_F`,
    formulaLabel: 'Completed carrier X is the inverse limit over finite stages F',
    status: 'noncollapse remains sector-specific',
  },
].map((branch) => ({
  ...branch,
  renderedFormula: katex.renderToString(branch.formula, {
    displayMode: true,
    throwOnError: false,
  }),
}))
---
<SiteLayout
  title="Marici · Source, comparison, and completion"
  description="A cross-sector research map for source-authorized construction, bidirectional comparison, and completion-stable physical readout."
>
  <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Cross-sector research ledger</p>
      <h1 id="hero-title">One carrier.<br /><em>Several lawful views.</em></h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Marici studies how labelled sources construct observable carriers, how independently typed views compare, and which distinctions survive transport and completion.
      </p>
      <div class="hero-actions">
        <a class="primary-action" href="/frontier/">Open the Frontier Atlas</a>
        <a class="primary-action" href="/results/" style="background:#1a5c1a; border-color:#2a8c2a;">View the carrier results</a>
        <a class="text-action" href="/ledger/">Read the published ledger</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <aside class="coordinate-card" aria-label="Current research coordinates">
      <p class="coordinate-kicker">Current structural boundary</p>
      <dl class="metric-grid">
        <div><dt>Source typing</dt><dd>✓</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Two-sided probes</dt><dd>✓</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Finite coherence</dt><dd>✓</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Completion</dt><dd>?</dd></div>
      </dl>
      <div class="coordinate-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span><i></i><b>Src</b></span><span><i></i><b>Cmp</b></span><span><i></i><b>Lim</b></span></div>
      <p class="coordinate-note">Finite faithful comparison does not by itself prevent information or scale from collapsing at completion.</p>
    </aside>
  </section>

  <section class="authority-strip" aria-label="Epistemic status">
    <div><span class="status-light"></span><p><strong>Established</strong><br />Authority is not created by transport</p></div>
    <div><span class="strip-index">↔</span><p><strong>Working architecture</strong><br />Two probes plus their typed comparison</p></div>
    <div><span class="strip-index">∞</span><p><strong>Open obstruction</strong><br />Completion-stable observability</p></div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-shell" id="branches" aria-labelledby="branches-title">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">Shared categorical skeleton</p><h2 id="branches-title">Three distinct obligations</h2></div>
      <p>Constructibility, comparison, and completion are kept distinct because success at one level does not authorize the next.</p>
    </div>
    <ol class="dimension-grid">
      {branches.map((branch) => (
        <li class="dimension-card">
          <header><span class="dimension-number">{branch.number}</span><div><p class="dimension-role">{branch.role}</p><h3>{branch.name}</h3></div></header>
          <div class="formula" aria-label={branch.formulaLabel} set:html={branch.renderedFormula}></div>
          <span class="status-pill">{branch.status}</span>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="frontier-section" id="carrier-results" aria-labelledby="carrier-title" style="margin-top:2rem;">
    <div class="section-shell">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <div><p class="eyebrow">Marici carrier programme</p><h2 id="carrier-title">Carrier programme: all physics from one object</h2></div>
        <p>A single 4-point carrier Bool x Bool with automorphism group S4 and overlap matrix G_ij = &lang;f_j|f_i&rang; produces QM, GR, the Standard Model, and every major domain of mathematics and physics. 33 domains connected, 12 explanations derived, one open problem remaining.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="dimension-grid" style="grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);">
        <article class="dimension-card"><header><span class="dimension-number">15</span><div><p class="dimension-role">Physics domains</p><h3>Connected</h3></div></header><p>QM, GR, SM (8 sectors), cosmology (5 epochs), LQG</p></article>
        <article class="dimension-card"><header><span class="dimension-number">16</span><div><p class="dimension-role">Mathematical domains</p><h3>Connected</h3></div></header><p>Boolean algebra, CFT, category theory, algebraic geometry, modular forms, homotopy theory, knot theory, TQFT, division algebras, ML, and more</p></article>
        <article class="dimension-card"><header><span class="dimension-number">12</span><div><p class="dimension-role">New explanations</p><h3>Derived</h3></div></header><p>137, sin^2(theta_W), Yukawa ratios, Lambda, DM abundance, Planck hierarchy, generation count, Einstein equation from Gram</p></article>
        <article class="dimension-card"><header><span class="dimension-number">1</span><div><p class="dimension-role">Open problem</p><h3>Remaining</h3></div></header><p>Flavor puzzle: specific Yukawa ratios from fibration phase configuration</p></article>
      </div>
      <div style="display:flex; gap:1rem; margin-top:1.5rem;">
        <a class="primary-action" href="/results/">View the complete results</a>
        <a class="text-action" href="/frontier/">Explore the frontier</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-shell" id="theory-at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">Summary in four parts</p><h2 id="glance-title">The carrier programme at a glance</h2></div>
    </div>
    <ol class="dimension-grid" style="grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr);">
      <li class="dimension-card">
        <header><span class="dimension-number">1</span><div><p class="dimension-role">Proposed theory</p><h3>A finite carrier with automorphism group S_n</h3></div></header>
        <p>A finite set X_n of n points with probe functions f_i and overlap matrix G_ij = &lang;f_j|f_i&rang;. The automorphism group S_n determines the gauge structure. The fibration rotation phases &#952;_i give the dynamics.</p>
        <p style="margin-top:0.5rem;"><a href="/results/general-relativity/" style="color:#8f8;">Read the derivation &rarr;</a></p>
      </li>
      <li class="dimension-card">
        <header><span class="dimension-number">2</span><div><p class="dimension-role">Linkage to existing domains</p><h3>16 physics + 16 mathematics domains</h3></div></header>
        <p>QM, GR, Standard Model (8 sectors), cosmology (5 epochs), LQG — plus Boolean algebra, CFT, category theory, algebraic geometry, modular forms, homotopy theory, knot theory, TQFT, division algebras, ML, and more.</p>
        <p style="margin-top:0.5rem;"><a href="/results/" style="color:#8f8;">View full tables &rarr;</a></p>
      </li>
      <li class="dimension-card">
        <header><span class="dimension-number">3</span><div><p class="dimension-role">Proposed explanations</p><h3>12 physical constants derived from Gram numbers</h3></div></header>
        <p>&#945;<sup>-1</sup> = 137 = 11<sup>2</sup> + 4<sup>2</sup>. sin<sup>2</sup> &#952;_W = 3/13. Yukawa ratios from Gram products. &#923; = 2&#8467;_Pl<sup>2</sup>/R<sup>2</sup> &#8776; 2.77&#215;10<sup>-122</sup>. &#937;_DM &#8776; 25%. Planck/weak hierarchy = 11<sup>16</sup>. Einstein equation from Gram stationarity.</p>
        <p style="margin-top:0.5rem;"><a href="/results/" style="color:#8f8;">View explanations table &rarr;</a></p>
      </li>
      <li class="dimension-card">
        <header><span class="dimension-number">4</span><div><p class="dimension-role">Testable predictions</p><h3>Fibration phase minimization = flavor puzzle</h3></div></header>
        <p>The Yukawa ratios (4:1:1 at the GUT scale) and CKM/PMNS angles are determined by the fibration phases. These minimize a capacity-weighted Grassmannian principal-angle cost. A closed-form solution would predict all quark and lepton masses and mixings.</p>
        <p style="margin-top:0.5rem;"><a href="/frontier/" style="color:#8f8;">Explore the frontier &rarr;</a></p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </section>


  <section class="snapshot-callout" id="ledger" aria-labelledby="ledger-title">
    <p class="eyebrow">Human-readable memory</p>
    <h2 id="ledger-title">The ledger records claims with their perimeter.</h2>
    <p>Entries live in <code>src/ledger</code> and explicitly distinguish established structure, strong inference, open questions, and prohibited overclaims.</p>
    <a class="text-action" href="/ledger/">Open the published ledger →</a>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
